            "target_entity_instance": "Sagar",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "In contrast, coastal blocks like Sagar and Namkhana receive lower average rainfall (approx. 1,546 mm). The lack of freshwater dilution in these areas leads to hyper-salinity during summer months, which can be lethal for many inland fish species and stunts production growth. Production in Kakdwip plummeted from 10,998 MT to 5,575 MT over ten years. The lower rainfall means that when cyclonic storms push seawater inland, there is insufficient rainwater to \"wash\" the salinity out of the soil and ponds, leading to long-term habitat degradation.",
