            "target_entity_instance": "southern coastal frontline",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Extreme Weather (Cyclones). Breaching of embankments; permanent soil and water table contamination. Infrastructure Debt: Constant need for reconstruction; reliance on government relief. These consequences prove that a \"one-size-fits-all\" management framework is no longer viable. The West Bengal Inland Fisheries Policy (2023) must differentiate between \"Productive Adaptation\" in the north and \"Survival Support\" in the southern coastal frontline to prevent a total socio-ecological collapse.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
